{
 "_howto": "One entry per payer. toc_url points at the payer Transparency in Coverage table-of-contents (index) JSON, which links every in-network MRF. direct_mrf_urls skips discovery for known files. Leave toc_url empty to skip that payer. Indexes are republished monthly with the month in the file name: bump the date in each toc_url at every refresh. UHC: index for UnitedHealthcare Insurance Company (the national fully-insured book), chosen from the payer's blob list at transparency-in-coverage.uhc.com/api/v1/uhc/blobs/. Aetna: files resolve from the always-current manifest https://mrf.healthsparq.com/aetnacvs-egress.nophi.kyruushsq.com/prd/mrf/AETNACVS_I/ALICSI/latest_metadata.json (5,697 deduped in-network files for Aetna Life Insurance Company on 2026-10-27); the first 80 are listed here and the run limit slices them. Cigna: the toc_url is the signed link from https://www.cigna.com/static/mrf/latest.json and expires, so re-read that manifest at every refresh. Elevance Anthem BCBS: one national index on S3 (status at /status.json on the same host), about 4 GB uncompressed, parsed as a stream. Humana: as of October 2026 Humana's published location sits behind a bot wall and third-party trackers report no current files found (none for August 2026), so it stays unconfigured until a readable index exists. Hospital MRFs (source_type=hospital) can be added later with the same shape.",
